# Retrieval-precision dataset for the seed library (cell80/cells).
# One case per line: {id, query, expected, category}.
#   expected   — acceptable cell id, or a list of acceptable ids.
#   category   — "direct" (uses the cell's own vocabulary),
#                "paraphrase" (natural rewording that avoids the cell's tag words),
#                "adversarial" (deliberately tricky / known-brittle for token overlap).
# The paraphrase + adversarial rows are the point: a .cell is only useful if findable
# when the user does NOT speak the library's vocabulary. These gate roadmap item 3
# (type-led index). Extend freely — keep at least a few paraphrases per cell.

